        "id": "tomb-of-the-spider-queen",
        "name": "Tomb of the Spider Queen"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Genji excels on Maps like Cursed Hollow, Hanamura Temple, or Garden of Terror, on which he can utilize his superior mobility to quickly engage and disengage using impassable terrain to his advantage. Doing so allows him to surprise the enemy team's backline from an unexpected angle. On smaller Maps like Battlefield of Eternity or Tomb of the Spider Queen, that require good waveclear, Genji's options are rather limited and make him a suboptimal pick. On Braxis Holdout, however, he can use his superior mobility to gank the offlane. Furthermore, Deflect can be used to great effect against the Boss on Braxis Holdout, whose fast Attack Speed causes Deflect to inflict heavy damage against it."
